ok   S: Delta(X) has the single edge a-b
ok   S: xc != 0, so <<a,b>> and <<c>> do not annihilate each other
ok   S: u = (alpha+xi)a + (beta+xi)b + (xi/2)w + (gamma-xi/2)c
ok   S: P_c = 2 ad_c^2 - ad_c satisfies P_c(u) = phi(u) c with phi(u) = gamma - xi/2
ok   S: coefficient vectors of phi(u), phi(au), phi(bu), phi(xu) as printed
ok   S: phi(au) = (beta - xi)/8, so phi(au) = 0 gives beta = xi
ok   S: phi(bu) = (alpha - xi)/8, so phi(bu) = 0 gives alpha = xi
ok   S: phi(u) = gamma - xi/2, so phi(u) = 0 gives gamma = xi/2
ok   S: phi(u) = phi(au) = phi(bu) = 0 iff (alpha,beta,xi,gamma) = xi(1,1,1,1/2)
ok   S: at such u, phi(xu) = -xi; so all four vanish only at u = 0
ok   S: determinant of the four vectors = -1/64 (cross-check, not stated in the paper)
