ok   S: a = c/2 + 2xc - 4a(xc)
ok   S: b = c/2 + 2xc - 4b(xc)
ok   S: c^2 = c != 0, so S^2 != 0
ok   S: exchanging a and b (fixing x, c) is an automorphism (cross-check, not stated in the paper)
ok   S: the multiplication algebra has dimension 16 (cross-check, not stated in the paper)
